title: Liberals Propose a Non-Confidence Motion
subtitle: The End of the Cooperative Coalition?
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1932 and month = 8 and party_names.ccf = 'PFLP'
priority: 2
max-visits: 1

= LPS Non-confidence Motion

The defections of the PPS MLAs have not gone unnoticed by the Liberals. Jimmy Gardiner's LPS is now moving for a motion of no-confidence against the Conservative Party and their Independent allies. The choice now lays with us whether Anderson's government survives. 

- @lps_no_confidence: Let's collapse the Cooperative Coalition government now
- @lps_confidence: Vote against the motion

@lps_no_confidence
choose-if: support_cooperative_coalition = 0
call: set_next_election_time

# set_next_election_time seems to be snap elections

= Snap Elections

The motion of no-confidence has passed. Now, the CPS will be entering an election burdened by the Depression. Our own party has much to gain; perhaps we may overcome the Conservatives as the official opposition? 

@lps_confidence
choose-if: support_cooperative_coalition = 1
on-arrival: workers_ccf -= 1; farmers_ccf -= 1; old_middle_ccf -= 4; new_middle_ccf -= 5;

= Anderson Holds steady

Thanks to the support of the [+ party_names.ccf +], Anderson's government manages to pass the LPS no-confidence motion. LPS-aligned newspapers are now unloading a heap of criticism at the PFLP for upholding Anderson's government. 